From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OAN Messaging <messaging@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:32:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(notifications): send SMS rows through the OAN Messaging
 Service

When oan_messaging_connector is configured on the site, _send_sms_row hands the row to
queue_sms (purpose transactional, source_reference grievance:<grievance>:<event>): the
connector sends it after commit with a fixed key, retries safely and polls delivery.
The row becomes "Queued with OAN" and links its OAN Message, instead of reading Sent on
hand-over; a message OAN cannot queue (too long for one SMS, bad number) fails the row.
Without OAN, Frappe's own sender and its fail-closed checks are unchanged.

Adds oan_messaging_connector to required_apps, the oan_message field and status
option, counts handed-over SMS in the ticket form, fetches the connector in CI\n(repository variable OAN_MESSAGING_CONNECTOR_REPO), and five tests.
